WEBVTT

00:14.250 --> 00:15.740
Senku.

00:16.890 --> 00:20.220
You're standing here alone, which means...

00:23.300 --> 00:26.500
We won, didn't we?!

00:26.810 --> 00:28.660
Yeah, Chrome.

00:28.660 --> 00:31.310
All thanks to your inspiration.

00:31.310 --> 00:35.130
I managed to make it through with 
the tenacity of a cockroach.

02:19.940 --> 02:24.860
Now, as the science tag team, 
we need to revive everyone.

02:26.230 --> 02:27.960
That'll take careful planning, too.

02:28.240 --> 02:31.880
If we don't play our cards right, 
we'll end up starving to death.

02:37.200 --> 02:39.030
I <i>am</i> getting hungry.

02:42.770 --> 02:44.050
Food!

02:44.050 --> 02:45.390
Amaryllis!

02:49.430 --> 02:50.510
So heavy...

02:51.760 --> 02:52.770
Power!

02:52.770 --> 02:54.110
Taiju!

02:59.710 --> 03:00.470
Cooking!

03:00.470 --> 03:01.740
Francois!

03:06.100 --> 03:08.330
Time to eat!

03:09.780 --> 03:11.160
It's so good!

03:13.640 --> 03:18.130
Unfortunately, our beloved cell phone's 
battery is on its last breath.

03:18.910 --> 03:22.090
Ruri called, but it died right after.

03:23.000 --> 03:25.100
You all doing okay?

03:25.390 --> 03:28.010
The earpiece was even more noisy.

03:28.010 --> 03:29.890
It was a call from the mainland, after all.

03:30.950 --> 03:33.320
She called to check up on us, huh?

03:33.320 --> 03:35.650
No wonder she was the priestess!

03:36.360 --> 03:41.040
But supposing they called us 
because they're worried,

03:41.040 --> 03:42.610
how would calling from the mainland help?

03:42.610 --> 03:44.470
Wouldn't they only get in our way?

03:45.850 --> 03:49.000
She called just for her own peace of mind?

03:49.000 --> 03:51.320
Ruri would never do that.

03:51.320 --> 03:54.750
For eighteen years, 
she's endured all kinds of worries

03:54.750 --> 03:57.040
for the sake of the people.

03:57.450 --> 03:58.460
You're right.

04:00.270 --> 04:02.810
Did you see how he trusts her and 
shows off how well he knows her?

04:02.810 --> 04:07.720
Is this Ruri girl Chrome's 
girlfriend or ex or something?

04:07.720 --> 04:11.740
No, I'm told that she is 
Senku-sama's former wife.

04:11.740 --> 04:13.140
What?!

04:13.430 --> 04:16.110
When did you get married, Senku?!

04:16.110 --> 04:18.780
Just for three minutes! 
We got divorced right away.

04:18.780 --> 04:19.950
What?!

04:19.950 --> 04:22.320
When did you get divorced, Senku?!

04:22.320 --> 04:24.790
I just said we got divorced right away!

04:22.540 --> 04:23.810
Wait, what?

04:23.810 --> 04:26.910
What is this Senku-Ruri-Chrome relationship?

04:27.260 --> 04:31.390
Well, you see, it's a stupidly long story.

04:32.930 --> 04:36.810
In any case, Ruri's trying 
to get in touch with us.

04:36.810 --> 04:38.040
We need to hear her.

04:38.520 --> 04:43.120
The Perseus's equipment might 
allow bidirectional communication.

04:43.120 --> 04:44.050
That's it!

04:44.440 --> 04:48.090
It should just barely reach, but...

04:56.900 --> 05:00.750
Those assholes made a damn mess!

05:00.750 --> 05:02.560
They didn't even know what 
they were dealing with!

05:02.560 --> 05:06.460
Now's not the time to be getting all salty.

05:02.810 --> 05:05.510
Bastards!

05:06.460 --> 05:10.240
Actually, I've never seen Senku truly angry.

05:10.240 --> 05:12.900
No, I get angry. I'm not a saint.

05:12.900 --> 05:14.330
I'm just too busy to.

05:14.900 --> 05:17.530
It'll take several weeks 
to restore everything.

05:17.530 --> 05:20.170
In that case, I'll begin
working on the mess hall.

05:20.170 --> 05:21.530
Already?!

05:21.530 --> 05:23.340
So very capable! I love it!

05:24.800 --> 05:27.320
We're gonna slap Kaseki and the others awake

05:27.320 --> 05:29.800
and get everything fixed up 
quick with everyone's help.

05:29.800 --> 05:30.950
It'll be fine.

05:30.950 --> 05:34.390
We're gonna be throwing revival 
fluid on everyone anyway.

05:36.880 --> 05:39.370
We have the petrification device.

05:39.370 --> 05:44.090
Let's take the Perseus on a victory cruise!

05:53.400 --> 05:57.430
Every time I'm revived, there's a 
brutal amount of work waiting for me.

05:57.430 --> 05:59.170
Brutal!

06:03.590 --> 06:07.840
<i>Right below the ship is where Yo's statue is.</i>

06:15.110 --> 06:16.350
Kirisame...

06:16.350 --> 06:17.690
She's an enemy, isn't she?

06:17.690 --> 06:20.740
What do we do? Do we revive her, or...

06:20.740 --> 06:22.520
Wreck it immediately!

06:22.520 --> 06:25.190
You're way too quick to resort to murder!

06:25.760 --> 06:27.950
And you're too quick in 
the opposite direction!

06:30.640 --> 06:34.030
She was merely being deceived by Ibara.

06:45.320 --> 06:46.690
What do you want to ask me?

06:47.680 --> 06:50.880
There's a reason I'm among the 
first you woke up, isn't there?

06:51.240 --> 06:52.950
Yeah, you're right.

06:52.950 --> 06:57.750
You know where they dumped the statues 
from the inner palace, don't you?

07:01.430 --> 07:03.110
Ginro's injuries...

07:04.150 --> 07:05.980
Are they really going to heal?

07:11.390 --> 07:14.450
The revival fluid's repair ability is no joke.

07:28.090 --> 07:30.130
G-Ginro...

07:30.770 --> 07:32.220
Kinro!

07:37.200 --> 07:38.250
Guys...

07:41.630 --> 07:43.450
K-Koha—

07:44.250 --> 07:46.330
Thank you!

07:47.330 --> 07:50.320
Kohaku-chan!

07:54.200 --> 07:56.810
Yup, Kinro's back to his old self.

07:56.810 --> 07:58.740
He's all better.

08:15.220 --> 08:18.530
No fair! Why Senku?!

08:18.530 --> 08:21.430
I want some of that, er, I mean...

08:19.990 --> 08:21.430
Oh, right.

08:21.690 --> 08:26.450
Kirisame-chan, you think they're 
in a legit relationship, don't you?

08:27.780 --> 08:30.100
I don't think that's what that hug was about.

08:30.570 --> 08:31.850
Not between those two.

08:41.890 --> 08:45.280
Nothing beats a cola after a job well done!

08:47.680 --> 08:52.790
Oarashi-sama here is gonna turn you 
into dust with his miracle power!

08:52.790 --> 08:54.260
You must think you're funny!

08:54.260 --> 08:56.510
What about you is such a miracle?

08:56.510 --> 08:59.430
Do you mean to say "mental"?

09:00.120 --> 09:02.370
How dare you?!

09:02.930 --> 09:04.170
Well, then...

09:04.170 --> 09:05.270
Ready...

09:07.130 --> 09:08.190
Aye!

09:11.890 --> 09:15.780
Magma, show them what the 
people of the sea are made of!

09:17.070 --> 09:18.660
I heard what you did, Ginro.

09:18.660 --> 09:21.840
You were severely injured, 
and yet you risked your life to—

09:21.840 --> 09:24.290
Aw, man! It's true, though!

09:24.610 --> 09:27.830
Being stabbed by Ibara 
was part of my plan, too.

09:27.830 --> 09:30.750
I'm great, don't you think?

09:31.130 --> 09:32.600
Ginro, you...

09:32.600 --> 09:34.320
Kinro, Ginro...

09:35.220 --> 09:37.630
Have you seen Senku and his team?

09:41.290 --> 09:42.640
Pipe down.

09:42.640 --> 09:44.170
Is it coming?!

09:44.170 --> 09:45.030
Found them.

09:45.030 --> 09:45.840
There!

09:46.420 --> 09:48.950
Drink with us, science team!

09:48.950 --> 09:50.480
You're working too hard.

09:52.680 --> 09:55.870
Here we go! We got a signal!

09:54.570 --> 09:57.740
Our communication device is fixed!

09:59.440 --> 10:03.720
Again, how the hell can we hear 
anything if you don't shut up?

10:10.020 --> 10:11.040
<i>Senku?</i>

10:12.090 --> 10:14.500
Yeah, can you hear me, Ruri?

10:15.140 --> 10:17.920
Thank goodness! I finally reached you.

10:18.210 --> 10:20.860
We can share our happy memories later.

10:20.860 --> 10:22.720
You need something, don't you? Shoot.

10:24.070 --> 10:26.200
Isn't this your first time 
talking to your former wife

10:26.200 --> 10:28.370
after all that's happened on the island?

10:28.370 --> 10:30.080
Is that really how you should talk to her?

10:30.080 --> 10:31.960
That's Senku for you.

10:32.380 --> 10:35.560
Senku, were you sending strange transmiss—

10:37.530 --> 10:39.070
There's interference on the transmission.

10:39.540 --> 10:40.950
By some other strong signal.

10:40.950 --> 10:42.450
Some other signal?

10:42.450 --> 10:45.080
There shouldn't be any other humans here.

10:46.030 --> 10:48.010
Does that mean...

10:51.290 --> 10:52.570
Morse code?

10:52.570 --> 10:54.170
Nope, that's not it.

10:55.520 --> 10:56.590
A human voice.

10:57.070 --> 10:58.030
Yeah.

11:02.980 --> 11:07.360
<i>Twelve million eight hundred thousand meters.</i>

11:07.360 --> 11:08.560
<i>One second.</i>

11:10.810 --> 11:12.310
No! The petrification device!

11:15.610 --> 11:17.650
Yeah, I know.

11:17.650 --> 11:20.320
Keep it away from the speaker 
even if it kills you.

11:22.960 --> 11:25.690
Why-Man's position is finally clear now.

11:26.080 --> 11:28.040
He's trying to destroy us.

11:28.660 --> 11:30.780
This is obvious intent to harm.

11:30.780 --> 11:33.290
I don't get it. Why by communication?

11:33.770 --> 11:35.400
This is insane!

11:35.400 --> 11:38.070
Twelve million eight 
hundred thousand meters?!

11:38.070 --> 11:42.220
What's up with that ridiculously 
huge, specific number?

11:42.740 --> 11:45.640
Twelve million eight 
hundred thousand meters...

11:49.450 --> 11:51.980
is the diameter of Earth.

11:54.890 --> 11:58.610
No, that's not the real question.

11:59.120 --> 12:00.650
That's not it.

12:01.100 --> 12:02.060
Yeah...

12:03.370 --> 12:04.620
This voice...

12:05.070 --> 12:06.440
Senku...

12:06.440 --> 12:07.500
It's your voice.

12:07.500 --> 12:11.900
Twelve million eight hundred thousand meters.

12:11.900 --> 12:13.080
One second.

12:17.360 --> 12:20.240
This is exhilarating!

12:26.990 --> 12:30.560
The voice behind the mystery 
transmissions is Senku's?

12:30.560 --> 12:32.520
I'm scared! I'm so scared!

12:32.520 --> 12:34.420
I'm getting goosebumps!

12:34.420 --> 12:36.420
Wh-Wh-What's going on?!

12:36.420 --> 12:39.520
Is Senku the one who was talking to us?

12:39.520 --> 12:42.130
So who's the Senku who's here with us now?

12:42.130 --> 12:43.620
You're wrong!

12:43.620 --> 12:46.390
Senku could never be a bad guy!

12:46.390 --> 12:48.830
Such inspiringly sloppy reasoning.

12:49.060 --> 12:51.750
It must be a smartphone recording!

12:51.750 --> 12:54.910
Sadly, I don't have a smartphone,

12:54.910 --> 12:58.590
and I ten billion percent have 
no memory of recording that.

12:58.590 --> 13:00.250
Senku's twin conspiracy theory.

13:00.250 --> 13:01.560
A doppelgänger?

13:01.560 --> 13:03.630
Senku the time traveler?

13:05.160 --> 13:09.080
Don't be rude. Baseless speculation 
is tantamount to fantasy.

13:09.080 --> 13:10.040
Am I right?

13:10.480 --> 13:12.500
Why-Man is out to get us.

13:12.500 --> 13:14.520
He'll be in contact with 
us again soon enough.

13:14.830 --> 13:16.810
And he'll eventually mess up.

13:17.800 --> 13:19.530
Tea time at a time like this?!

13:19.530 --> 13:21.530
How are you so chill?

13:23.880 --> 13:26.610
We got another transmission!

13:26.610 --> 13:29.660
He's repeating it on regular intervals.

13:32.080 --> 13:36.460
<i>Twelve million eight hundred thousand meters.</i>

13:36.460 --> 13:37.960
<i>One second.</i>

13:39.470 --> 13:41.010
It's the same as the last time.

13:41.010 --> 13:42.530
Even in its timbre.

13:43.160 --> 13:46.670
As a former sonar operator, I'm sure of it.

13:47.210 --> 13:51.600
It has the same uncanny valley 
quality as a Vocaloid.

13:52.510 --> 13:53.810
It's a synth voice.

13:55.770 --> 13:57.410
H-H-How?!

13:57.410 --> 13:59.400
In the stone world?!

14:00.560 --> 14:05.330
<i>How</i> isn't much of an issue right now.

14:05.330 --> 14:07.000
The fact is that it's being done.

14:07.000 --> 14:08.440
The real question is <i>why</i>?

14:08.440 --> 14:11.290
Why are they communicating 
with a synth voice?

14:11.290 --> 14:16.230
From there, we might be able to figure 
out who they are and where they are.

14:16.580 --> 14:22.280
It seems clear that Why-Man-chan is a 
naughty boy trying to petrify us all...

14:22.280 --> 14:23.610
But why the transmission?

14:23.610 --> 14:25.800
Why is it imitating Senku-chan's voice?

14:27.040 --> 14:28.440
Transmissions...

14:28.440 --> 14:30.110
Senku's voice...

14:30.110 --> 14:31.050
Imitations?

14:33.220 --> 14:38.820
When you finished off Ibara, you used 
your voice over the radio, didn't you?

14:40.090 --> 14:43.290
Isn't that what they're imitating?

14:43.660 --> 14:48.170
I can't tell if this Why-Man
 is smart or stupid.

14:48.490 --> 14:51.530
Isn't he the one who made all 
this crazy science stuff?

14:51.530 --> 14:56.660
Why is that petrification 
device on this island, anyway?

14:56.660 --> 14:58.200
Yeah, that's the thing.

14:59.770 --> 15:04.100
If anyone knows the history of the device, 
they might also know Why-Man's identity.

15:04.100 --> 15:05.760
I-I remember!

15:05.760 --> 15:08.090
I mean, I don't know anything...

15:08.470 --> 15:10.760
But the shape of the petrification device...

15:15.560 --> 15:17.790
Now that we know Why-Man is our enemy,

15:17.790 --> 15:20.760
our job as the battle team 
is no longer to investigate.

15:21.140 --> 15:24.730
It's to train for the inevitable battle.

15:26.490 --> 15:30.700
We just defeated the Petrification 
Kingdom! This is even scarier!

15:46.590 --> 15:47.600
They're evenly matched!

15:47.600 --> 15:49.730
They're both incredible.

15:50.350 --> 15:51.630
You're strong.

15:51.630 --> 15:56.180
You were holding back the last 
time we fought, weren't you?

15:57.010 --> 15:58.990
I wasn't going easy on you.

15:58.990 --> 16:01.080
I would never be so disrespectful.

16:01.080 --> 16:04.840
I apologize. I was simply not accustomed 
to moving around in a dress.

16:06.490 --> 16:07.990
No!

16:09.770 --> 16:14.160
I don't want to be part of all this craziness!

16:20.290 --> 16:21.960
Who's this statue?

16:21.960 --> 16:25.710
A person from long ago that Taiju-chan 
brought back from the sea floor.

16:28.670 --> 16:30.530
Th-This person's arm...

16:30.530 --> 16:32.880
Is this a wound? A tattoo?

16:32.880 --> 16:34.490
Could you take a look at it?

16:35.390 --> 16:36.540
Look!

16:36.540 --> 16:39.220
It looks like a symbol of 
the petrification device!

16:39.700 --> 16:43.420
Oh, that's the one that broke 
off as I was carrying him.

16:44.550 --> 16:46.940
The surface can't have 
deteriorated yet, then.

16:46.940 --> 16:49.700
We might be able to repair 
it with the revival fluid.

17:05.930 --> 17:10.070
It's been a while since I've seen all the 
crackling when they're being repaired.

17:10.070 --> 17:13.130
The surface of the statue 
is degraded with time.

17:13.670 --> 17:15.860
It can't be restored, so it falls off.

17:18.080 --> 17:20.620
His fragments are thinner than ours.

17:20.620 --> 17:23.480
He must be from a few hundred years ago.

17:23.930 --> 17:26.730
Are you telling me I've been 
brought back to life after I was

17:27.150 --> 17:29.150
attacked by that strange light?

17:29.370 --> 17:30.510
That's right.

17:30.510 --> 17:33.080
That's exactly what we want to hear about.

17:33.810 --> 17:36.270
Strange travelers, you have my gratitude.

17:36.270 --> 17:37.200
Thank you.

17:37.470 --> 17:39.410
Yeah, we can skip this part.

17:39.410 --> 17:41.610
Just tell us about the device.

17:43.120 --> 17:46.520
No way! Save me!

17:43.890 --> 17:45.410
Stop running, Ginro!

17:56.060 --> 17:57.930
Master!

17:59.300 --> 18:00.850
Master!

18:08.950 --> 18:11.420
Forgive me, Master!

18:11.420 --> 18:15.740
I was petrified, 
but now that I have returned,

18:15.740 --> 18:18.210
the enemy will not have their way!

18:18.620 --> 18:20.020
Wh-What?

18:20.020 --> 18:22.200
Is he on our side? He's strong.

18:22.640 --> 18:25.490
What? Who did you think he was?

18:25.490 --> 18:27.080
He's just a scummy loser.

18:27.080 --> 18:29.350
No! That's not true!

18:32.690 --> 18:34.450
Eh?

18:36.420 --> 18:40.840
Man, do I really look like that 
important person from way back?

18:41.210 --> 18:44.000
We <i>are</i> distant relatives.

18:44.000 --> 18:47.290
It wouldn't be an overstatement 
to say I'm his reincarnation.

18:47.290 --> 18:52.970
I guess you could serve me 
in his place for now, right?

18:51.500 --> 18:54.420
Is it just me, or is he being scummy again?

18:52.970 --> 18:56.070
There must be a reason you were 
brought back to me, right?

18:54.420 --> 18:57.740
That's what he does, every chance he gets.

18:57.740 --> 18:59.300
He has a track record.

18:59.300 --> 19:02.720
How was he so fetching while 
he was cross-dressing?

19:02.720 --> 19:05.770
Come on, you must know, right, Matsukaze-kun?

19:05.770 --> 19:09.960
Tell Senku all about the 
petrification device's history!

19:11.370 --> 19:14.070
Then speak I shall.

19:15.340 --> 19:18.240
This island was once peaceful.

19:18.710 --> 19:21.400
Then, one day, they rained down upon us.

19:33.060 --> 19:35.440
Countless so-called "petrification devices."

19:36.090 --> 19:38.150
Nightmares raining down from the heavens.

19:40.460 --> 19:41.750
I knew it!

19:41.750 --> 19:43.410
It came from above!

19:43.670 --> 19:48.250
That's plenty of useful information!

19:48.250 --> 19:49.890
Let's get moving!

19:51.680 --> 19:54.880
Weren't we in the middle 
of hearing about the past?!

19:54.880 --> 19:57.380
We'll fill the rest in with science!

19:59.120 --> 20:01.190
They're gone already...

20:04.090 --> 20:05.180
Here we go!

20:05.420 --> 20:09.220
Is that the weapon we used 
against Tsukasa's army?

20:09.630 --> 20:12.320
That's the thing that gathers sound.

20:12.320 --> 20:13.940
The shock cannon.

20:14.380 --> 20:16.010
What are we using that for?

20:16.960 --> 20:21.820
Gathering sound and gathering 
radio waves work the same way.

20:21.820 --> 20:25.390
This parabolic antenna's gonna 
help us trace the signal

20:25.390 --> 20:27.390
Mr. Why-Man's been pissing on us.

20:27.200 --> 20:29.200
m 0 0 l 246 0 l 246 80 l 0 80

20:27.200 --> 20:29.200
Parabolic Antenna
acquired!!

20:29.860 --> 20:34.250
<i>Twelve million eight hundred thousand meters.</i>

20:34.250 --> 20:35.580
<i>One second.</i>

20:37.640 --> 20:41.250
Our measurement separation's 
too small to tell the difference.

20:41.250 --> 20:44.340
They're well beyond the 
surface or the atmosphere.

20:45.400 --> 20:47.690
I don't get it. What's going on?

20:47.690 --> 20:50.420
The enemy's really far?

20:51.210 --> 20:52.720
On the other hand...

20:52.720 --> 20:57.390
The rotation of the planet will 
move us a few thousand kilometers.

20:57.390 --> 20:58.770
Enough to barely figure it out.

20:59.070 --> 21:01.990
In other words, they aren't 
infinitely far away or anything.

21:03.190 --> 21:05.360
So they're super close?

21:05.360 --> 21:06.570
Which is it?!

21:09.090 --> 21:13.500
Well, then, based on the results 
of our triangulation...

21:13.990 --> 21:18.380
The enemy is a few hundred 
thousand kilometers above.

21:19.450 --> 21:22.080
That's right. Why-Man is...

21:23.980 --> 21:25.730
on the Moon.

21:26.630 --> 21:27.570
The...

21:27.570 --> 21:28.430
...Moon?!

21:28.850 --> 21:31.220
It's moving in conjunction with the Moon.

21:31.530 --> 21:32.770
There's pretty much no doubt.

21:33.060 --> 21:35.310
Is that even possible?!

21:35.310 --> 21:40.060
But how are we supposed 
to deal with them there?

21:41.430 --> 21:45.820
Leave them to their own devices, 
and they'll eventually ruin us.

21:53.070 --> 21:54.910
Wait, wait, wait...

21:54.910 --> 21:57.020
I have a bad feeling about this again.

21:57.020 --> 21:59.310
I mean, I can't see how this 
could be anything but bad.

21:59.310 --> 22:00.460
Yeah...

22:00.460 --> 22:02.560
I definitely know what's coming.

22:02.560 --> 22:05.550
You're taking this primitive stone world...

22:07.190 --> 22:10.840
We're going to the Moon!

22:10.840 --> 22:14.930
I knew it!

23:49.320 --> 23:52.410
<b>Treasure Island</b>

23:51.950 --> 23:54.930
<b>Next Episode</b>

23:51.970 --> 23:54.930
<b>Treasure Island</b>

